ed Rick was inducted  into the Officer Candidate Hall of Fame  at Fort Benning Georgia and Dan went to  see Rick received this great honor there  and it turned out was the last time they  were ever together but after a day of  you know ceremonies and camaraderie and  I have to say quite a bit of drinking  it's a  there's a fair amount of alcohol in this  story but a Rick turned to Dan and and  in his very typical way he always asked  questions he never gave orders he simply  asked questions and he turned to Dan and  said are we all that we could have  become this was late in their careers  dan had had a heart attack Rick was  suffering from prostate cancer at a time  when I'm sure most people would have  been entirely justified in resting and  retiring and simply settling down to  enjoy their remaining days  Rick was still trying to become more  than he had become he was questioning  whether they had achieved all that a  human being could achieve in their  remarkable laws and all I can say is  that on September 11th he did become all  that he could and that's something I try  to think about every day am i all that I  could have become can I do more with the  qualities that have been to study state  upon me and that to me in the end is the  message I take from Rick and one that I  hope will inspire many other readers as  well thank you  James Stewart is author Oh den of  thieves bloodsport and his latest heart  of a soldier it's published by Simon &amp;  Schuster on the web at Simon Says  dot-com

